      "writtenOn": "2023-04-18T21:25:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is a map of the entire pools types and counts. To get to this call above us in the stack we would be in `VulkanResourceProvider::findOrCreateDescriptorSet(map\u003cType, count\u003e dsDesc)`. However, the dsDesc in that call is just the types and counts for one individual descriptor set. To generate the map you have on the pool here you would need to iterate over the dsDesc and multiple all the counts by some kSetsPerPool value and create a second map.\n\nBut all the second map is used for is to pass into this factory where we immediately iterate over it to produce VkDescriptorPoolSizes. Couldn\u0027t we just skip that middle map and pass this factory the original dsDesc and an `int setsPerPool`. Then we just do that multiple when filling out poolSizes here?",
